      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem to add much complexity compared to the current patch though: instead of having \"this\" as argument to the new constructor, you just need to have each of the fields as argument. Or to make it shorter, a reference to \"this\", and separate arguments for each field that changes (queryCount, transactionId, expectUnicastResponse, burstCounter, isFirstBurst, queriesPerBurst, delayUntilNextTaskWithoutBackoffMs, timeBetweenBurstsInMs). Then I think all fields can be final.\n\nRight now this method modifies fields in one thread, and then they\u0027re read in another thread (for example in calculateTimeToRun). I think it\u0027s OK because it\u0027s always holding the lock, but that\u0027s very error-prone.\n\nSo doing it in another change LGTM, but this should be done ASAP because things like \"lastScheduledTask.config is different after getConfigForNextRun was called\" are very error-prone.",
      "revId": "d704b8cafbd325eb6b3200819005f0efe7c05774",
